  "orderInUnit": 8,
  "standard": "TRIG.IDENT.2",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "prompt": "An engineer studying an AC circuit meets the expression $1 - 2\\sin^2(\\omega t)$. Which single trig function is it equal to?",
  "answerType": "multiple-choice",
  "choices": [
    {
      "id": "A",
      "label": "$\\cos(2\\omega t)$",
      "correct": true
    },
    {
      "id": "B",
      "label": "$\\sin(2\\omega t)$",
      "correct": false
    },
    {
      "id": "C",
      "label": "$\\cos^2(\\omega t)$",
      "correct": false
    },
    {
      "id": "D",
      "label": "$-\\cos(2\\omega t)$",
      "correct": false
    }
  ],
  "primaryAnswer": "A",
  "alternativeAnswers": [],
  "acceptanceMode": "exact",
  "hint": "The cosine double-angle formula comes in three equivalent versions.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "The cosine double-angle formula comes in three equivalent versions."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "One of them is $\\cos(2\\theta) = 1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta$. Compare it with what you have."
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "With $\\theta = \\omega t$ the expression is exactly $\\cos(2\\omega t)$."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "The three forms of the cosine double-angle identity are $\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$, $2\\cos^2\\theta - 1$, and $1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta$.",
    "The expression matches the third form with $\\theta = \\omega t$.",
    "So $1 - 2\\sin^2(\\omega t) = \\cos(2\\omega t)$ — this is exactly how engineers show that the power in an AC circuit oscillates at twice the supply frequency."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Derive it if you forget it",
      "steps": [
        "Start from $\\cos(2\\theta) = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$.",
        "Replace $\\cos^2\\theta$ with $1 - \\sin^2\\theta$: $\\cos(2\\theta) = (1 - \\sin^2\\theta) - \\sin^2\\theta$.",
        "That simplifies to $1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta$ — you never have to memorise all three separately."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    "double-angle",
    "ac-circuit",
    "modelling"
  ],
